# Frontend rules

## Layout
```
frontend/src/
  main.tsx, App.tsx
  styles/tokens.css        # CSS variables from docs/design-spec.md (the only place hex values live)
  styles/global.css
  api/client.ts            # REST calls
  api/stream.ts            # SSE over POST (fetch-event-source)
  types/contracts.ts       # TS mirrors of docs/spec.md (events, cards, draft)
  state/chatStore.ts       # useReducer-based store: messages, cards, draft, phase, typing
  hooks/useChatSession.ts  # creates session, sends messages/actions, applies events
  components/layout/       # AppHeader, Breadcrumb, PageShell
  components/chat/         # ChatPanel, ChatHeader, ProgressStages, MessageList, UserBubble, BotBubble, TypingIndicator, SuggestionChips, Composer
  components/cards/        # ConfirmFieldsCard, MallPickerCard, OtpCard, DocumentChecklistCard, ReviewCard, SuccessCard
  components/draft/        # DraftPanel, DraftGroup, DraftRow, SourceBadge, ChecksList, BadgeLegend
  mocks/                   # fixtures + a mock event stream for running the UI without the backend
```

## Practices
- Match `docs/design-spec.md` exactly: tokens, sizes, radii, copy. Use `var(--token)`; never hard-code hex outside `tokens.css`.
- Components are presentational; all chat state lives in `chatStore`. Cards receive their payload + callbacks as props.
- Cards are keyed by `card_id`. A new `ui_card` event with an existing id replaces that card's payload in place (the card updates where it is in the conversation).
- Accessibility: real `<button>`, `<input>`, `<label>`; `aria-pressed` on toggle chips; `aria-live="polite"` on the message list; visible focus ring; touch targets ≥ 44px; 4.5:1 text contrast.
- Responsive: the two panels wrap below ~920px; chat first, draft second.
- `VITE_MOCK=1` runs the whole UI against `mocks/` with no backend, replaying the scripted demo flow from `design/prototype.dc.html`.
- Tests: Vitest + React Testing Library for the store reducer, every card and the draft panel.
